@startuml
' US-17 — Find a note.
' Activity — the search, and which answer it gave
' Sources: ../../../analysis/stories.md (US-17), ../../../specification/03-features.md (F-24)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor #333
  ArrowColor #333
}

start
:the library's form asks for the notes\nwhose name holds the text;

partition "the reader" {
  :the folders are walked for the names,\nsix levels down;
  note right
    The walk has a budget, and it says
    when it runs out.
  end note

  if (the walk finished in time?) then (yes)
    :the notes that were found are the answer;
    :the answer says — the folders were walked\njust now, six folders down;
  else (no)
    if (the index is built?) then (yes)
      :the index answers, and the answer says —\nthis is the index, of such a time;
    else (no)
      :what was found so far is the answer,\nand the answer says there may be more;
    endif
  endif
}

partition "the library's page" {
  :the notes are listed, each with the\nfolder it is in;
}

stop

note right
  F-24: the search says which answer it gave.
  A reader who is told "13 notes" should know
  whether the number is the truth or a copy of
  it.
end note
@enduml
